WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.080
Have you ever wondered how a country can be
hijacked?

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.660
How institutions can be subjected, perverted
and corrupted?

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.530
And perhaps most importantly, how to identify
the moment in which a democracy, after being

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.969
taken over, stops working?

00:00:12.969 --> 00:00:18.250
Dear viewers, for years these questions have
pervaded international politics... but especially

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:33.690
Latin American politics.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:54.829
In the last decades, numerous Latin American
leaders have taken control of their countries.

00:00:54.829 --> 00:00:59.230
Sometimes they did it through coups d'état...
but in many other occasions these dictators

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:01.719
came to power through democratic means.

00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:06.430
That is precisely the case of the Nicaraguan
President, Daniel Ortega.

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:13.260
My friends, here at VisualPolitik, we’ve
already told you about this political figure,

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.620
how he came to power, how he behaved and how
he was responsible for the huge strikes that

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:31.810
Nicaragua has gone through in 2018.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:36.780
Strikes that have been answered with a heavy
hand and which have led to terrible consequences:

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:41.820
more than 200 people have lost their lives,
hundreds have been detained and thousands

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:42.820
injured.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:47.780
Well, in this video, we’ll take a look at
another aspect of the events.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:51.680
This is the story of how a government managed
to take control of the state and make the

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.090
institutions work not for the country, but
for itself.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:02:00.720
This is the story of how a kind of political
mafia took control of Nicaragua.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.720
Listen up.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:16.719
The year is 2006, Daniel Ortega wins the Nicaraguan
presidential elections.

00:02:16.719 --> 00:02:21.590
After 16 years as the opposition, the Sandinista
leader returned to the country’s presidency.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:27.870
The precedents weren’t precisely good: his
first term as president between 1985 and 1990

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.359
was... terrible.

00:02:29.359 --> 00:02:36.189
Ortega left an economically and socially shattered
country.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:43.560
A country that went through a war, ended up
with a foreign debt 6 times bigger than its

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.749
GDP, and suffered from hyperinflation that
reached the astronomical figure of 33.547%

00:02:48.749 --> 00:02:49.749
by 1987.

00:02:49.749 --> 00:02:56.099
To give you an idea of the magnitude of the
disaster, in 1990 the per capita income of

00:02:56.099 --> 00:03:01.340
Nicaragua was 55% smaller than the country
had registered in 1978.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:10.329
In other words, compared to Daniel Ortega,
even the Kirchners would get good grades.

00:03:10.329 --> 00:03:18.659
Folks, Ortega's economic model was a huge
failure: the expropriations, the gigantic

00:03:18.659 --> 00:03:24.719
foreign debt, the unstoppable money printing
and his obsession with controlling the economy...

00:03:24.719 --> 00:03:37.610
led Nicaragua into an unsustainable situation
- And how wouldn’t it have, with that recipe!

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:42.139
And if we add the Contras conflict to all
of this, financed by the United States, the

00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:54.510
country was submerged in a complete disaster.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:58.499
By the way, for those of you who don’t know,
the Contras were paramilitary groups financed

00:03:58.499 --> 00:04:03.349
by Washington through selling weapons to Iran
when this country was in the middle of a war

00:04:03.349 --> 00:04:06.999
with Iraq, a country that was supposedly close
to Washington.

00:04:06.999 --> 00:04:09.099
In short, complete nonsense.

00:04:09.099 --> 00:04:15.349
So throughout the following decade the country
only had one mission: to recover from this

00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:18.750
mess.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:32.900
To do this, the following governments, starting
with that of Violeta Chamorro – by the way,

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:38.160
the first elected female Latin American president
– decided to turn the country’s political

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.370
and economic approach around.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:45.610
That is, to move from a centralized economy,
which was organized and directed by the state,

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:50.280
to a market economy.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:59.050
That’s how the Nicaraguan free trade zones
were born, as well as the policies to attract

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:04.200
foreign investment, which along with international
cooperation and especially the growing remittances

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:09.750
from abroad, allowed Nicaragua to get back
on track.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:23.900
But just a moment... because what these new
governments didn’t achieve was putting an

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.169
end to corruption...

00:05:26.169 --> 00:05:30.650
Thus, scandal after scandal, the feeling of
frustration, disappointment and deceit all

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:35.240
Nicaraguans felt – along with an opposition
who was willing to do almost anything to return

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.740
to power – fueled Ortega’s victory in
2006.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:52.310
And here, dear viewers, is where the new story
begins... especially because Ortega wasn’t

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:54.740
going to waste his return to power.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:06:00.860
This was his chance, his opportunity to dominate
Nicaraguan politics, finances and society.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:06.220
But to achieve this, and above all, to prevent
an electoral process from re-evicting him

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:11.770
from the presidency, he needed to seize political
power, with an armed force and economic power

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:12.770
monopoly.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:17.349
This is the strategy he set in motion and
the steps he took to achieve his purpose.

00:06:17.349 --> 00:06:21.120
Listen up.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:27.950
(POLITICAL POWER)

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:33.400
Obviously his strategy’s first goal was
to achieve political hegemony and social control...

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.000
by any means.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:40.080
This was very clear to Ortega from the beginning
and he launched a double tactic to achieve

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.439
it:

00:06:41.439 --> 00:06:46.830
First, by "invading" the institutions and
centralizing power, and then by limiting and

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.500
intimidating the opposition....

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:52.909
something for which fear is usually a very,
very effective ingredient.

00:06:52.909 --> 00:06:57.219
Therefore, shortly after arriving, Ortega
launched a paramilitary force composed of

00:06:57.219 --> 00:06:58.219
gang members.

00:06:58.219 --> 00:07:02.490
We’re talking about the shock groups, better
known in Nicaragua as the “Turbas”.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.389
("They are feared, and the people call them
mobs.

00:07:05.389 --> 00:07:10.159
They usually wear T-shirts that speak of love
and peace, wear helmets to hide their faces

00:07:10.159 --> 00:07:16.600
and move on motorcycles, they’re mostly
very violent young people."- Matilde Córdoba,

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:18.189
journalist in Managua.)

00:07:18.189 --> 00:07:19.909
Its objective?

00:07:19.909 --> 00:07:24.099
To intimidate the political opposition, to
frighten those who disagree with the government

00:07:24.099 --> 00:07:29.819
and to try to dismantle the opposition’s
demonstrations or concentrations with violence.

00:07:29.819 --> 00:07:34.320
Obviously, it isn’t an official force...
but they have the government’s protection.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.419
We’ll see how in a moment.

00:07:37.419 --> 00:07:42.139
( "We can say that a paramilitary force has
been set up in Nicaragua that is composed

00:07:42.139 --> 00:07:43.389
of gang members.

00:07:43.389 --> 00:07:47.600
Sometimes we get on a bus and a paramilitary
is watching us".

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:50.159
- Haydeé Castillo, Nicaraguan activist.)

00:07:50.159 --> 00:07:52.409
But, of course, it doesn’t end here.

00:07:52.409 --> 00:07:58.080
The next step to achieve total political control
is to take control of the state institutions.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:03.400
Now, how do you think he did it?

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:12.389
Well... first political decentralization had
to be ended, in this case municipal autonomy.

00:08:12.389 --> 00:08:18.020
Thus, in Nicaragua Ortega's political henchmen
have managed to dismiss mayors at will.

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:21.970
Something like... hey, if you have a political
rival, kick him out of the race, that way

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:26.509
you don’t only get rid of your opponents,
you also win loyal fans who, of course, don’t

00:08:26.509 --> 00:08:32.779
want to risk making you mad.

00:08:32.779 --> 00:08:38.329
The second step to institutional takeover
was to create and legitimize his own political

00:08:38.329 --> 00:08:41.779
organizations, in this case the "Citizen Power
Councils".

00:08:41.779 --> 00:08:46.950
These bodies, which supposedly involve community
participation, in practice have the objective

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:55.339
of creating a parallel political structure
that is recognized and controlled by the government.

00:08:55.339 --> 00:09:00.860
And the third, appoint and achieve the indefinite
permanence of his party associates in every

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:06.920
key state position: the Electoral Power, the
Judicial Power and the General Comptroller.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:10.340
And if an official protests... that's what
the mobs are for, right?

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:15.550
Do you want two examples proving what Ortega
achieved with this strategy?

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:16.550
Check it out.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:24.540
On the 
one hand, the Nicaraguan Constitution prohibited

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.750
the consecutive re-election of a president.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:31.149
So Ortega would have completed his term in
2011.

00:09:31.149 --> 00:09:37.920
However, as Hernández did in Honduras, Ortega
managed to get the Constitutional Chamber

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:44.670
of the Supreme Court, composed mostly of Sandinista
magistrates, to declare article 147 as inapplicable,

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:48.610
which is the one that prevented the presidential
consecutive re-election.

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:53.889
In exchange, yes, the magistrates’ positions
were ensured, for life.

00:09:53.889 --> 00:09:58.079
Doesn't sound like a bad reward, right?

00:09:58.079 --> 00:10:03.180
On the other hand, in 2011… fraud suspicions
were so intense that both the European Union

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:07.390
and the Organization of American States concluded
that they weren’t sure of the results.

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:10.910
Do you know who controlled the Electoral Power?

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:16.480
Exactly, Ortega had made sure that his followers
could do and undo whatever they wanted.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:20.870
In fact, in the following elections, the 2016
ones… they didn’t even split and the ruling

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:23.360
party took full control of the process.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:24.360
But... wait a moment...

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:28.020
you may be thinking, Simon, wasn’t there
a scandal because of it?

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:33.310
Well, let's say that the president had made
sure that practically every major media station

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:37.410
in the country was controlled by his family
or associates.

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:42.399
("The Ortega Family monopolizes the media
in Nicaragua" Diario las Américas)

00:10:42.399 --> 00:10:52.459
Mobs, the occupation of institutions and the
media, this is the political side, but there’s

00:10:52.459 --> 00:10:54.100
more.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:57.080
(THE FORCE MONOPOLY)

00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:03.610
Of course, for as much as he holds political
power, if a dictator doesn’t hold the force,

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.660
he’s taking a huge risk.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:09.620
This was very clear to our protagonist, so
the second pillar of this strategy was to

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:15.050
take over the police and the army.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:18.870
To do so, he took advantage of his majority
in the National Assembly.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:22.680
As soon as he got to power Ortega pushed a
reform that placed the ability to appoint

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:28.040
new faculties of the National Police and the
Army of the Republic in his hands.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:33.880
Then, taking advantage of these new possibilities,
he placed relatives and loyal people directly

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.690
in charge of these institutions.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:39.870
For example, the police are directed by his
own Father in Law, Francisco Díaz...

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:44.310
so he can get the police to look the other
way when the mobs act... and when the opposition

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:49.970
strikes, repression, repression and more repression.

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:56.230
Because when the mafia holds the power, it
won’t be easy to get them to let go.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.070
But... politics, public force...

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:02.610
there’s a third element missing.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:07.139
(THE ECONOMIC POWER)

00:12:07.139 --> 00:12:13.130
The third pillar in this strategy was to achieve
economic power, for 3 reasons:

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:17.649
first, to prevent Nicaraguan capital from
supporting an alternative; second, to get

00:12:17.649 --> 00:12:22.290
resources with which to carry out Ortega’s
plans, and third, perhaps the most important

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:25.029
point, to fill his pockets.

00:12:25.029 --> 00:12:32.180
Throughout this time, corruption has been
brutal... to such an extent that today the

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.460
Ortega-Murillo family are millionaires, true
millionaires.

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:38.370
See, they’ve taken over the media, they
hold high positions in the state; they’ve

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:42.209
even taken over oil import and distributions
in Nicaragua!

00:12:42.209 --> 00:12:46.529
They’ve put themselves in charge of the
investment promotion agencies...

00:12:46.529 --> 00:12:48.680
with a plan that we could describe in this
line

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:50.300
Want to invest in Nicaragua?

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:53.670
Great we’ll make it happen but you have
to give me a commission.

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:54.970
You know, for the country.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:13:00.649
They’ve also reached agreements with businessmen:
apparently by getting loyalty and envelopes

00:13:00.649 --> 00:13:03.780
in exchange for privileges.

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:09.880
A clear example of this way of doing things
was the agreement made to build the Interoceanic

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:14.839
Canal, a seemingly unsuccessful project...
but in which the government reached an under-the-table

00:13:14.839 --> 00:13:18.150
agreement with Wanj Jinm, the Chinese developer
working on it.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:23.320
At first the state kept half of the profits...
and then with a last minute change, it became

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:24.340
1%.

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:27.630
(Ironic) Obviously, the businessman haggled
at the last minute…

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:29.470
such skill, not even Messi can haggle like
that.

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:34.620
In short, my friends, the fact is that with
political power, with brute force, and with

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:39.079
economic power, Daniel Ortega became the owner
and lord of Nicaragua.

00:13:39.079 --> 00:13:40.990
And, well, also a billionaire.

00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:46.590
And just in case, in the last election, in
2016, he presented Rosario Murillo, his wife,

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:47.709
as Vice President.

00:13:47.709 --> 00:13:51.980
So, everything stays in the family.

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:59.389
My friends, this process is very similar to
what happened in Venezuela, it is, so to speak,

00:13:59.389 --> 00:14:01.110
the dictator’s manual.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:06.110
And the question we can ask ourselves is,
can we really pretend that Nicaragua is still

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.449
a democracy?

00:14:07.449 --> 00:14:11.050
